# Role Selection and Pursuit Priority

Operational reference: `BLUEPRINT.md` §138
(`BORA_ROLE_SELECTION_AND_PURSUIT_PRIORITY_STANDARD_V1`) locks the full
doctrine for which roles Career OS should actively search for,
prioritize, and spend application effort on. This file is a pointer, not
a restatement — read §138 (and the sections it cross-references: §5, §6,
§7, §19-21, §132, §135, §136) before acting on discovery, comparison-pool,
freshness, remote-authenticity, or pursuit-priority questions.

## Governance boundary (the one invariant worth restating here)

This doctrine governs Pursuit Truth and Package Truth only — discovery
priority, pursuit urgency, and how a serious role is presented for Bora's
decision. It never governs Qualification Truth, Employer Truth, Candidate
Truth, or Match Truth, all of which remain owned entirely by
`job_analysis.py`, `job_decision.py`, and the existing deterministic
requirement/evidence-match/qualification-gate/recruiter-threshold
pipeline, unchanged.

Do not convert, under any circumstance:

* `UNKNOWN` -> `SUPPORTED`;
* `UNKNOWN` -> `NONE`;
* adjacent experience -> direct experience;
* functional overlap -> qualification;
* good location -> qualification;
* a fresh posting -> qualification;
* remote authenticity -> qualification;
* institutional affinity -> qualification;
* network access -> qualification.

## Quick-reference vocabulary (full definitions in §138, not here)

* Comparison-pool discovery bands: A+ / A / B / C (§138.1) -- "do not
  actively target" 2-4/3-5/5+/Senior/Lead/Principal/Manager is a
  discovery/pursuit-economics rule, never an automatic qualification
  REJECT; the existing mechanical recruiter-threshold guard in
  `job_decision.py` remains authoritative and unchanged.
* Freshness bands: `VERY_FRESH` / `FRESH` / `AGING` / `STALE_LEANING` /
  `UNKNOWN` (§138.5) -- Bora-specific pursuit urgency, never a universal
  employer-hiring-probability claim, and never a modification of Employer
  Truth. `STALE_LEANING` never means closed or unqualified.
* Locked discovery windows (§138.5): `GOLD_WINDOW` = 0-7 days;
  `STRETCH_WINDOW` = 8-14 days; `FAR_STRETCH_WINDOW` = 15-21 days;
  `EXCEPTION_ONLY_WINDOW` = 22+ days; `UNKNOWN_WINDOW` when employer posting
  date is not reliable. `EXCEPTION_ONLY_WINDOW` is not a hard exclusion: an
  unusually strong, strategically exceptional, first-party verified-live role
  may still deserve pursuit. Missing/unreliable employer posting date stays
  `UNKNOWN` / `UNKNOWN_WINDOW`; never substitute `discovered_date` or
  `date_first_seen` as the employer posting date. These are governance/
  presentation labels only, never schema/runtime enums or employer cutoffs.
* Locked work-format preferences (§138.4): actively favor verified `REMOTE`,
  `CONTRACT`/contract-to-hire/temporary, and `PART_TIME` opportunities in
  discovery; combinations such as remote + contract or remote + part-time get
  strong tiebreak priority among otherwise comparable opportunities. Boston/
  Greater Boston contract, temporary, and part-time roles also get positive
  preference even when hybrid or onsite. These are discovery biases, not hard
  filters or a fixed Lane A/B/C hierarchy: they never override fit,
  authorization, first-party actionability, Candidate/Match/Qualification
  Truth, or suppress an unusually strong accessible full-time/hybrid/onsite
  opportunity.
* Remote authenticity: `VERIFIED` / `LIKELY_LEGITIMATE` / `UNCLEAR` /
  `HIGH_RISK` / `CONFIRMED_FRAUD` / `N/A` (§138.7) -- doctrine vocabulary
  for human/model assessment only; not a schema enum or runtime field.
* Serious-role output standard (§138.8): Bora Fit, Comparison Pool,
  Freshness, Discovery Window, Location/Work Arrangement, First-Party Actionability, Remote
  Authenticity, Authorization, Opportunity Value, Pursuit Economics, and
  a Final Verdict (`PURSUE - DEEP` / `PURSUE - CONTROLLED HIGH-QUALITY` /
  `PURSUE - EFFICIENT` / `WATCH` / `REJECT`). No numeric score, no fake
  probability, no point system, ever.

**Disambiguation (§138.8):** every §138.8 label is presentation
vocabulary for Pursuit Truth only -- never a value of, or synonym for,
`Job.decision`, `Job.lane`, `role_status`, or `source_verification_status`,
and never to be written into those persisted/runtime fields (e.g.
Freshness `STALE_LEANING` != `role_status=POSSIBLY_STALE`; Final Verdict
`WATCH`/`REJECT` do not redefine the existing `Job.decision` enum even
where the label text coincides).

## Stop rule

This doctrine lock does not itself authorize runtime implementation --
no new schema, enum, runtime scoring, lane value, decision value,
database field, remote-fraud classifier, automated fraud declaration, or
job-search automation change is pre-authorized by §138. A separate,
explicitly earned architecture audit under §133's build-economy gate is
required before any of that is built.
